; WHO 4 four-zone central unit (#0#1..#0#4, #0#21) vs 99-zone (#0) and zone (Z, #Z, #Z#1)
; translation across the gateway fleet (OpenWebNet-HA/MyHOME#994, PR #1000).
;
; Covers:
;   1. Central setpoint writes (*#4*#0#C*#14*TTTT*M##) for M=1/2/3 across #0#1..#0#4,
;      #0#21 (ZA=2, ZB=1 = 0x15, BTicino U1809C pp. 54-55), and #0.
;   2. Zone setpoint writes across plain Z (1, 3), 99-zone #Z (#1, #3), and BTouch #Z#C
;      (#1#1, #3#1) -- exposing Gen A (#C -> 00) and Gen B (MH200N / F453 / F453AV NACK
;      on direct Z writes).
;   3. Central weekly programs 1101..1103 / 2101..2103 / 3101..3103, 3100 restore,
;      scenarios 1201..1203 vs holiday 115/315, OFF/protection 303/203/103/302/202/102,
;      season 1/0, 311, event-only 110#/210#/310#, and zone mode writes (303/102/202/1/0).
;   4. Central & zone status / dimension queries (*#4*#0#1..#0#4##, #0#21, #0, DIM 14/12/0/20).
;   5. Inbound PIC telegrams (2-digit $17/$18 and 3-digit $017/$018) from BTicino 4695
;      v01.01.03 (C0 status + diagnostic flags, C2 controlled-zone read, BF pump) and
;      external Master Pump Actuator B7 00 31 01 -> *#4*#0#1*20*0##.

; 1. Central setpoint writes (DIMENSION 14)
